From: overpressure <overpressure@pico4>
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: H.264's end of stream with a NULL address on IRIS2

The firmware (VIDEO.VPU.1.0-00093) takes an exception when a stop command ends an H.264 stream with
the driver's 0xdeadb000 address. With NULL, which the driver uses for firmware up to 1.0.87, the
stream ends cleanly. HEVC, VP9 and VP8 end cleanly with the old address, so they keep it.
---
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/vcodec/venus/vdec.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/vcodec/venus/vdec.c
@@ -576,7 +576,8 @@
 		 * avoids misapplying this quirk and breaking VP9 decode on SC7280.
 		 */
 
-		if (IS_IRIS2(inst->core) && is_fw_rev_or_older(inst->core, 1, 0, 87))
+		if (IS_IRIS2(inst->core) &&
+		    (is_fw_rev_or_older(inst->core, 1, 0, 87) || inst->fmt_out->pixfmt == V4L2_PIX_FMT_H264))
 			fdata.device_addr = 0;
 		else
 			fdata.device_addr = 0xdeadb000;
